Rationale: The claim has two material parts: (1) the Phillips Berlina is a neo-classic car that used stretched underpinnings, and (2) the underpinnings came from a car that set a new sales record for model year 1979. None of the evidence directly identifies the Phillips Berlina or its underpinnings. The search for the car that set a sales record in 1979 returned only information about kei cars and music albums, which are irrelevant. The search for the underpinnings of the Phillips Berlina also returned no relevant information. Therefore, the evidence is insufficient to support or contradict the claim, and further investigation is needed.
